This extension adds Bloodthief modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]Mod Loader automatically installed.[/summary]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Godot Mod Loader installs to the game folder, recognised by a "mod_loader.gd" file.[/*]
[*]Map mods with a ".map" file with a matching ".json" file install to the "maps" folder.[/*]
[*]Godot mods with a ".gd" file install to the "mods-unpacked" folder.[/*]
[*]Any other mod not described above installs to the "mods-unpacked" folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*][color=#ffff00][size=3][b][url=https://github.com/olvior/bloodthief-mod-loader]Mod Loader[/url]﻿﻿ will be automatically downloaded and installed.[/b][/size][/color][/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Bloodthief mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Godot Mod Loader:

Recognised when the archive contains a "mod_loader.gd" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Map Mods:

Levels for the game's map loader. A map is a pair of files sharing one name, kept together in a folder named after the map.

[code]
MyMap.zip
└── Author-MyMap\
    ├── mymap.map
    ├── mymap.json
    └── textures\
[/code]

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a file with the ".map" extension that has a ".json" file of the same name beside it.
    - The folder holding the pair is kept as the installed map folder, so name it after the map.
    - A "textures" subfolder alongside the pair is installed with it.

  Installs to: "maps"

  Common mistakes:
    - Shipping the map file without its matching ".json" - the pair is what identifies a map, so a lone map file is not recognised and falls through to another installer.
    - Putting the map files at the archive root - the installer then has to invent a folder name from the archive filename.

========================================================================

Godot Mod:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".gd" file.

  Installs to: "mods-unpacked"

========================================================================

Fallback Installer:

The catch-all. Any archive that matched none of the installers above lands here and is copied across unchanged.

[b][color=#ffff00]NOTE: Landing in the fallback installer is a signal your archive layout needs fixing.[/color][/b]

  Requirements:
    - Reaching this installer usually means the archive was not laid out in a way Vortex recognised.
    - Vortex shows the user a notification when a mod installs through the fallback.

  Installs to: "mods-unpacked"

  Common mistakes:
    - If your mod lands here unintentionally, re-check the layouts above - users will see a fallback warning and may report the mod as broken.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives that contain a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with "ModuleConfig.xml") are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead, and none of the rules above apply.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]

